    "Description": "OpenSSH is an SSH protocol implementation supported by a number of Linux, UNIX, and similar operating systems. It includes the core files necessary for both the OpenSSH client and server.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* openssh: openssh: Information disclosure via shared compression side-channel (CVE-2026-106582)\n\n* openssh: openssh: Arbitrary file write via directory traversal during sftp recursive copy (CVE-2026-106552)\n\n* openssh: OpenSSH: Credential disclosure via failed GSSAPI authentication (CVE-2026-106553)\n\n* openssh: openssh: Denial of service via oversized decompressed packets (CVE-2026-106585)\n\n* openssh: openssh: Command injection via unvalidated command-line username (CVE-2026-106583)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
